{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1789784301,"nonce":"BBp7yAc46aY5HgA53JB+j0EH8QQ=","title":"a parameter assigned in an if-branch reads as the last branch's value after the join","message":"`static function f(?len:Int):Int { if (len == null) len = 10; return len; }`\nreturned 0 (the parameter register), and with an else branch the else\nbranch's value regardless of the condition. The if-statement join\n(mir/expr/dispatch.rs `lower_if_statement`) collected the symbols to phi\nonly from `func.locals`, which a parameter never has (parameters are seeded\ninto `register_types` and bound in `symbol_map`); the loop joins already\ncarried the same fallback to the register's type. The if-expression join\n(expr/conditionals.rs) had the same gap.\n\nEvery optional-parameter default (`if (pos == null) pos = 0`) hit this:\n`BytesInput`'s `len` stayed 0, so every read threw Eof.\n\nFixture: haxe-conformance/regressions/ParamReassignInBranch.hx.","files":null}]}